{"type":"text","timestamp":1782089908137,"sessionID":"ses_1133326f5fferY8263tLjfJvZ3","part":{"id":"prt_eecd5eeaa001NaHoFaV5w2wmv8","messageID":"msg_eecd59fe50015CvmXqJ62G0sVB","sessionID":"ses_1133326f5fferY8263tLjfJvZ3","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented a TypeScript MCP server for Brazilian soccer data per `TASK.md`.\n\n## What was built\n\n**Project structure**\n- `package.json` / `tsconfig.json` / `vitest.config.ts` — ESM TypeScript project with `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `csv-parse`, `zod`, `vitest`\n- `src/types.ts` — canonical domain model (`Match`, `Player`, `TeamStats`, `HeadToHead`, `Standing`)\n- `src/normalize.ts` — team-name normalization (state-suffix stripping, accent folding, legal-name aliases) + multi-format date parsing (ISO, DD/MM/YYYY, with/without time)\n- `src/loader.ts` — loads & normalizes all 6 Kaggle CSVs (23,954 matches, 18,207 players); cached lazily; data dir overridable via `BRAZILIAN_SOCCER_DATA`\n- `src/queries.ts` — pure query functions: `findMatches`, `headToHead`, `teamStats`, `findPlayers`, `standings`, `averageGoals`, `biggestWins`, `bestTeamRecord`, `competitionsForTeam`\n- `src/server.ts` — MCP server exposing 7 tools: `search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `team_statistics`, `search_players`, `competition_table`, `aggregate_stats`, `list_reference`\n- `src/index.ts` — stdio transport entry point\n- `tests/bdd.test.ts` — 23 BDD Given/When/Then tests covering all 5 required capabilities + normalization + MCP tool registration + data-coverage checks\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run typecheck` — clean\n- `npm run build` — clean (emits `dist/`)\n- `npm test` — **23/23 passing**\n- End-to-end stdio MCP session confirmed: `tools/list`, `list_reference`, and `head_to_head` (Flamengo vs Fluminense → 77 matches, 31/25/21 W/D/L) all return correct JSON-RPC responses\n\nRun with `npm start` (or `npm run dev` for tsx).","time":{"start":1782089903786,"end":1782089908134}}}
